Source: task-ai-desktop
Section: tasks
Priority: optional
Maintainer: AI Workspace Lab <ai-workspace-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/ai-workspace-lab/ai-desktop

Package: task-ai-desktop-core
Architecture: all
Depends:
 dbus-x11,
 xdg-utils,
 xdg-user-dirs,
 x11-utils,
 x11-xserver-utils,
 xauth,
 ca-certificates,
 fontconfig,
 fonts-noto-core,
 fonts-noto-cjk,
 fonts-noto-color-emoji,
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 adwaita-icon-theme,
 gvfs,
 gvfs-backends,
 libqt6core6t64,
 libqt6gui6,
 libqt6qml6,
 libqt6quick6,
 libqt6quickcontrols2-6,
 libqt6widgets6,
 qt6-qpa-plugins,
 libxcb1,
 libx11-xcb1,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: core runtime for the task-ai-desktop environment
 Provides the shared X11, D-Bus, XDG, font, icon, GVFS and Qt runtime needed
 by the task-ai-desktop session and its native components.

Package: task-ai-desktop-session
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, icewm, dbus-x11, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xorg
Description: ICEWM session integration for task-ai-desktop
 Starts the ICEWM session shell, installs user startup/menu helpers and
 provides the shared Xvfb headless-session entrypoint.

Package: task-ai-desktop-xdock
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-session, xdock, ${misc:Depends}
Description: XDock integration for task-ai-desktop
 Installs the XDock EWMH dock component and its task-ai-desktop path alias.

Package: task-ai-desktop-xlaunch
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-session, xlaunch, ${misc:Depends}
Description: XLaunch integration for task-ai-desktop
 Installs the XLaunch Menu and full-screen application launcher and its
 task-ai-desktop path aliases.

Package: task-ai-desktop-apps
Architecture: all
Depends:
 task-ai-desktop-session,
 xfce4-terminal,
 thunar,
 thunar-volman,
 chromium | firefox-esr,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: desktop applications for task-ai-desktop
 Provides the recommended terminal, file manager and web browser while
 keeping application choices separate from the core desktop session.

Package: task-ai-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends:
 task-ai-desktop-core,
 task-ai-desktop-session,
 task-ai-desktop-xdock,
 task-ai-desktop-xlaunch,
 task-ai-desktop-apps,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xorg, lightdm
Description: lightweight AI Workspace X11 desktop meta-package
 Installs the complete ICEWM desktop combination: XDock, XLaunch,
 xfce4-terminal, Thunar, Chromium or Firefox, fonts, icons, GVFS, D-Bus and
 the Qt/X11 runtime. It does not select a display manager.

Package: task-ai-desktop-vps
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop, xvfb, x11vnc, dbus-x11, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xorg, xrdp, xpra, novnc, websockify
Description: VPS profile for task-ai-desktop
 Adds the Xvfb and X11VNC path for a headless VPS without a physical display
 or GPU. Xorg with XRDP or xpra remains available as an optional transport.

Package: task-ai-desktop-container
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop, xvfb, x11vnc, dbus-x11, tini, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: novnc, websockify
Description: OCI container profile for task-ai-desktop
 Adds Xvfb, X11VNC, D-Bus and init integration for an OCI container without
 systemd, LightDM or a physical display. noVNC and websockify are optional.

Package: task-ai-desktop-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: git, gh, python3, golang, nodejs, npm, jq
Description: development-tool recommendation for task-ai-desktop
 Keeps the development toolchain separate from the runtime desktop. Install
 the Home-Ubuntu version matrix explicitly when a build or development host
 needs Git, GitHub CLI, Terraform, Ansible, Python, Go, Node.js, pnpm, jq or
 Google Cloud CLI.
